November 4, 2015
Thomas Schingle
Operations Chief
2101 O’Neil Avenue, Room 104
Cheyenne, WY 82001
RE:   Emergency Response Facility
Dear Mr. Schingle:
Plan One / Architects along with TCA Architecture is pleased to provide the Cheyenne Fire and
Rescue Department with the following Statement of Qualiﬁcations for the proposed
Emergency Response Facility Project.
Our proposed team aﬀords the City of Cheyenne the opportunity to engage the services of a
nationally recognized ﬁre station design ﬁrm, TCA Architecture, together with the  enthusiasm
for, and commitment to, Wyoming design Plan One/Architects delivers to its clients.
While the project will be lead  by Plan One from the interview through the 11‐month walk‐thru,
our teaming arrangement will ensure that the design experts from TCA Architecture will be
front and center during the programming, planning, and schematic design phases of the
project.  This assures the project’s stakeholders they will be actively engaged with a team who
fully understands the nuances of these types of facilities while simultaneously establishing a
relationship with  a ﬁrm who has a truly vested interest in working with the City.
Looking to the future, we see our new Cheyenne oﬃce as a cornerstone of growth for our ﬁrm
and look forward to developing strong working relationships with the City.  If you have
questions regarding the information contained within this Statement of Qualiﬁcations, please
do not hesitate to contact me at 307.352.2954.
Sincerely,

Charles E. Van Over, AIA
President
