### Page 4 of 33

```text
Incorporated in 1985, Plan One/Architects has grown to one of the largest Wyoming based architectural ﬁrms
in the state.  Plan One/Architects employs 17 people in three oﬃces with ﬁve Registered Architects and a LEED
Accredited Professional on staﬀ.
While many large regional Firms choose to specialize in a speciﬁc area of architecture, such as medical,
correctional or educational, Plan One has chosen to specialize in providing design work that ﬁts the needs of
clients located within the State of Wyoming.  By being ﬂexible and responsive, Plan One has been able to
successfully design Projects including correctional, educational, and historic preservation.  This ability to adapt
to whatever a Project requires gives clients in the State the distinct advantage of working with a Wyoming
based ﬁrm whose reputation is at stake with each and every project it undertakes.  We take all of our projects
very seriously, as we know that in Wyoming reputation is the key to continued work.
Recognizing that, while Plan One has designed several successful ﬁre stations in the past, our experience might
not be as recent as others in the area, we have enlisted the services of TCA Architecture•Planning from Seattle,
Washington, to ensure that the most modern ﬁre station design principles are incorporated into the project.
TCA Architecture has been involved in the planning and design of ﬁre service facilities since 1960. With the
planning and design of over 250 ﬁre stations throughout the US to their credit, their award‐winning ﬁrm
understands the ﬁre service culture, and how this inﬂuences facility design.  As a result of their years of eﬀort,
TCA is recognized in the national ﬁre community as one of the leading ﬁre facility design ﬁrms in the country.
Rounding out our consultant team will be Cator, Ruma & Associates, providing mechanical, electrical, and
Information Technology engineering services; Martin/Martin Wyoming for structural engineering; Western
Research and Development for civil engineering; and J.R. Conkey & Associates of Roseville, California for
professional cost estimating.
Due to the specialized nature of TCA’s design experience this would be our ﬁrst time working with their ﬁrm,
however, we understand what to expect in this kind of an arrangement  due to our successful collaborations
with other nationally recognized ﬁrms in the ﬁelds of criminal justice and medical facilities planning.  With that
exception, Plan One/Architects has teamed successfully with each of the other consultants listed below on past
projects and can attest to their professional abilities from ﬁrst‐hand experience.
